00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:47.040
Yes.

356
00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:52.760
So in this episode, Halloween, Michael is told that he must fire someone during the

357
00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:55.400
month of October due to cutbacks at Dunder Mifflin.

358
00:13:55.400 --> 00:14:01.620
But in true Michael fashion, he waits until the very last day of October, which also happens

359
00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:02.420
to be Halloween.

360
00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:04.880
He also has no idea who to fire.

361
00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:05.980
He has not made a decision.

362
00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:11.120
He spends the entire episode trying to figure out what to do while the rest of us are dressed

363
00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:13.040
in our costumes for the Halloween party.

364
00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:14.520
I love that.

365
00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:15.560
I love that.

366
00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:19.520
I love the juxtaposition of that someone is going to get fired while wearing a ridiculous

367
00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:20.040
costume.

368
00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:20.400
Yes.

369
00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:22.360
And they're going to have to go home fired in that outfit.

370
00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:25.320
Well, I have a fast fact about this episode.

371
00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:28.400
Fast fact number one, Greg Daniels wrote this episode.

372
00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:34.060
And he told me that the inspiration for this episode was that he had always wanted to do a

373
00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.020
