374
00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:44.480
the employee, he felt like we always see stories of people being fired and how they're wrestling

375
00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:45.720
with having been fired.

376
00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:48.520
But he was like, you never see what it does to the boss.

377
00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.900
That's the genius of Greg Daniels right there.

378
00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:51.380
Absolutely.

379
00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:56.440
Well, the problem that this plot presented for Greg was that he was going to have to

380
00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:57.700
fire someone on the show.

381
00:14:57.740 --> 00:15:01.720
He was going to have to pick a Dunder Mifflin employee to be part of the plot.

382
00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:06.900
Well, he couldn't fire any of the series' regular characters because we all had contracts.

383
00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:12.320
And he didn't want to fire any of the supporting cast, even though at this point, you guys still

384
00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:15.140
did not have your full-time contracts, right?

385
00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:15.440
No, we didn't.

386
00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:17.480
We didn't become series regulars till Booze Cruise.

387
00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:19.740
So listen, we were all on the chopping block.

388
00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:23.140
Were you a little worried when you saw this episode?

389
00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.540
Well, Greg didn't have any intention of losing them.

390
00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:28.120
He didn't want to lose anyone in the warehouse.

391
00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:33.020
But he also told me he didn't want to hire someone new that you'd never seen on the

392
00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:34.280
show just to fire them.

393
00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:37.000
He felt like those stakes would feel very manufactured.

394
00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:42.740
So he turned to our two background actors, Creed and Devin.

395
00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:43.860
Creed and Devin, yeah.

396
00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:48.400
And he was like, well, these guys are very well-established on the show at this point.

397
00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:53.040
And this is where I'd like to know what happened.

398
00:15:53.040 --> 00:16:00.100
Because I know the end of this story, which is that Greg found out that Devin had a theater

